<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Cultures</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Cultures of Europe</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 14 cultures of Europe, from the Cucuteni–Trypillia culture to the Vikings. Read their profiles, then answer.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Europe">Open the cultures &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the cultures from 1 (the earliest to begin) to 7 (the latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Hallstatt culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Bell Beaker culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Yamnaya culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Cucuteni–Trypillia culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Minoan civilisation</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Mycenaean civilisation</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Nuragic civilisation</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right homeland next to each culture. Their profiles will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Cucuteni–Trypillia culture</li><li>Yamnaya culture</li><li>Minoan civilisation</li><li>Bell Beaker culture</li><li>Nuragic civilisation</li><li>Mycenaean civilisation</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>From the Carpathian Mountains to the Dniester and Dnieper, about 350,000 km², centred on present-day…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Crete, with settlements and strong influence on Thera, Kythera, Melos, Kea and Rhodes in the Aegean and at…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Mainland Greece, above all the Peloponnese, Attica and Boeotia, with Crete from c</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The Pontic–Caspian steppe between the Southern Bug, Dniester and Ural rivers, in present-day Ukraine and…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Western and central Europe</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The island of Sardinia, with about one nuraghe every three square kilometres</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p><b>Cucuteni–Trypillia culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The culture spread from the eastern Carpathians to the Dnieper, and in its middle phase its people built some of the largest settlements in Eurasia, a few with as many as three thousand structures.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Yamnaya culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;‘Yamnaya’ is an archaeologists’ label from a Russian word meaning ‘related to pits’, after the pit graves under burial mounds that mark this herding culture of the steppe.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Minoan civilisation</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;From about 1900 BCE the people of Bronze Age Crete built Europe’s first palaces, at Knossos, Phaistos and Malia: complexes of courts, storerooms and workshops that organised the island’s wealth.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose two of these cultures that lived at the same time. What did they have in common, and what set them apart?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Europe. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Cultures of Europe</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Cucuteni–Trypillia culture <span>c. 5050 BCE – c. 2950 BCE</span></li><li>Yamnaya culture <span>c. 3300 BCE – c. 2600 BCE</span></li><li>Minoan civilisation <span>c. 3100 BCE – c. 1100 BCE</span></li><li>Bell Beaker culture <span>c. 2800 BCE – c. 1800 BCE</span></li><li>Nuragic civilisation <span>c. 1800 BCE – 238 BCE</span></li><li>Mycenaean civilisation <span>c. 1600 BCE – c. 1100 BCE</span></li><li>Hallstatt culture <span>c. 1200 BCE – c. 450 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Cucuteni–Trypillia culture <span>1: From the Carpathian Mountains to the Dniester and Dnieper, about 350,000 km², centred on present-day…</span></li><li>Yamnaya culture <span>4: The Pontic–Caspian steppe between the Southern Bug, Dniester and Ural rivers, in present-day Ukraine and…</span></li><li>Minoan civilisation <span>2: Crete, with settlements and strong influence on Thera, Kythera, Melos, Kea and Rhodes in the Aegean and at…</span></li><li>Bell Beaker culture <span>5: Western and central Europe</span></li><li>Nuragic civilisation <span>6: The island of Sardinia, with about one nuraghe every three square kilometres</span></li><li>Mycenaean civilisation <span>3: Mainland Greece, above all the Peloponnese, Attica and Boeotia, with Crete from c</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the profiles.</p></section></div></details>
